This file belongs to the project: the blueprint wrote it once, and its updates leave it alone. It adds to `AGENTS.md` what a coding agent needs to know about this project alone, such as its architecture, the commands of its own checks and what to watch for in its tests.

## Where things are

[% if stack != 'generic' %]- [% if stack == 'home-assistant' %]The integration is in `custom_components/{= ha_domain =}/`, its manifest and version in `custom_components/{= ha_domain =}/manifest.json`, the HACS metadata in `hacs.json`[% elif stack == 'php' %]The app is in `lib/`, its metadata, version and supported Nextcloud versions in `appinfo/info.xml`[% elif project_type == 'github-action' %]The action is defined in `action.yml` and runs `{= python_package =}.py`[% elif project_type == 'python-package' %]The package is in `src/{= python_package =}/`, its metadata and version in `pyproject.toml`[% elif stack == 'node' %]The package is in `src/`, its metadata and version in `package.json`[% elif stack == 'container' %]The image is built from `Dockerfile`, with the application in `app/`[% endif %].
[% endif %]- `README.md` documents installation, configuration and use, `docs/` holds the pages of the website, and `CHANGELOG.md` lists the changes of every release.[% if stack == 'container' %]
- `scripts/check.sh` builds the image and runs its self-test.[% elif stack != 'generic' %]
- The tests are in `[% if stack == 'node' %]test/[% else %]tests/[% endif %]`; `scripts/check.sh` runs every check.[% endif %]
